* Alternative: resistive-zero peaking. The reference sets the 14 GHz peak with switched
* capacitor banks between the source nodes; this design uses one fixed capacitor pair
* (CZP/CZN) around a resistor RZ0 that peak-code switches shunt with RZ1, RZ2 or RZ3,
* moving the degeneration zero instead of adding capacitance. Shunt peaking 200 pH.
